{"id":"q01","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"puzzle","question":"A bat and a ball cost $1.10 in total. The bat costs $1.00 more than the ball. Does the ball cost 10 cents?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The ball does not cost 10 cents.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The ball costs 5 cents.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The intuitive approach of subtracting $1.00 from $1.10 gives $0.10 for the ball.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Many people quickly give the 10-cent answer.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"If the ball were 10 cents, the bat would be $1.10 and the total $1.20, not $1.10.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The 10-cent answer fails the stated conditions.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Setting ball = x and bat = x + 1.00 yields 2x = 0.10, so x = 0.05.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"With a 5-cent ball and $1.05 bat, the total is $1.10 and the bat is exactly $1.00 more.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The ball being 10 cents is the correct answer.","confidence":0.02,"lean":1,"theta":0.0314,"phi":-0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":-1.0,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":-1.0,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":-0.4,"relatio